preConditionHook:
// HAS THE CORRECTION LASTED LONG ENOUGH RELATIVE TO THE LEG IT IS CORRECTING?
// Brooks's duration rule of thumb (V21-01), used to hold off a with-trend
// continuation entry until the correction has had time to finish: "about half
// as many bars" is his phrasing, so 0.5 is the default reading and the
// source's own example was a 20-to-30-bar bear channel.
//
// IDENTICAL BOTH SIDES, as the merge recorded it: this counts BARS, not
// direction. The leg and its correction are read off the pivot structure with
// no reference to which way either ran -- the most recent CONFIRMED pivot of
// either kind ends the leg and starts the correction, the most recent pivot
// of the OPPOSITE kind before it started the leg, and the two bars-ago
// numbers are the two durations. A pane that also wants a direction ANDs one.
//
// NOT CorrectionBarsFractionOfPattern, which is the same ratio measured
// against a different span: that rule anchors on SAME-KIND pivots (the
// pushCount-th swing low back, for a three-push bottom) and its long side
// reads the low pivots only, where this one takes the last leg spanned by
// two pivots of opposite kind and reads both series. They fire on different bars at every default, and at
// pushCount = 1 that rule is switched off by its own patternBars > 0 guard
// rather than degenerating to this one. DeepPullbackRetracementFilter is the
// DEPTH half of the same idea, measured in price; the two should be tested
// together.
//
// PIVOT SCAN, MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt, el_swing_output1.txt): the pivot
// bar is AT OR ABOVE the pivotStrength OLDER bars and STRICTLY ABOVE the
// pivotStrength NEWER bars -- bars-ago indexing, so the newer bars are the
// SMALLER kk and take the strict test, the older the at-or-above one;
// confirmation lag exactly pivotStrength bars; candidate offsets
// pivotStrength..lookbackBars - 1, the neighbourhood reaching pivotStrength
// bars past the window, so the deepest bar touched is
// lookbackBars - 1 + pivotStrength. Only the FIRST pivot of each kind is
// wanted, which is the smallest offset, carried by the -1 guard rather than a
// loop break -- EasyLanguage has no Break and the twin must scan the same
// bars.
//
// lookbackBars is PROMOTED: the merged parameters name only the fraction and
// the strength, but a pivot scan needs a window and this is
// CorrectionBarsFractionOfPattern's default so the two can be tuned together.
//
// -1 IS THE NO-PIVOT SENTINEL and the guards on it are load-bearing: a
// missing pivot must not read as a pivot at bar 0. An outside bar can in
// principle be both a high and a low pivot; that leaves hiBar1 == loBar1,
// corrBars stays -1 and the rule is simply false, which is the honest answer
// for a degenerate structure.
//
// Compared, never divided.
//
// Deepest bar touched: lookbackBars - 1 + pivotStrength.
hiBar1 = -1;
loBar1 = -1;
for (jj = (int)pivotStrength; jj <= (int)lookbackBars - 1; ++jj) {
    okHi = true;
    okLo = true;
    for (kk = jj - (int)pivotStrength; kk <= jj - 1; ++kk) {
        if (el_le(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (el_ge(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (kk = jj + 1; kk <= jj + (int)pivotStrength; ++kk) {
        if (el_lt(high[jj], high[kk])) okHi = false;
        if (el_gt(low[jj], low[kk])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && hiBar1 == -1) hiBar1 = jj;
    if (okLo && loBar1 == -1) loBar1 = jj;
}
corrBars = -1;
legBars = 0;
if (hiBar1 >= 0 && loBar1 >= 0) {
    if (hiBar1 < loBar1) {
        corrBars = hiBar1;
        legBars = loBar1 - hiBar1;
    }
    if (loBar1 < hiBar1) {
        corrBars = loBar1;
        legBars = hiBar1 - loBar1;
    }
}
adequate = (corrBars >= 0) && (legBars > 0) && el_ge((double)corrBars, correctionFraction * (double)legBars);
